164
00:05:40,536 --> 00:05:42,636
I'm sorry to interrupt.

165
00:05:43,436 --> 00:05:45,165
Can I share some words of encouragement before we wrap up?

166
00:05:45,166 --> 00:05:46,575
Sure. You can do that.

167
00:05:46,576 --> 00:05:48,075
- I was getting to that.
- For the students...

168
00:05:48,076 --> 00:05:49,305
- preparing to take the CSAT?
- Yes.

169
00:05:49,306 --> 00:05:50,745
- Right.
- Please go ahead.

170
00:05:50,746 --> 00:05:53,576
Dear teenagers who are preparing to take the CSAT this year.

171
00:05:53,976 --> 00:05:56,545
You've worked so hard. You're almost at the finish line.

172
00:05:56,546 --> 00:05:58,446
Keep trying to the end.

173
00:05:58,546 --> 00:06:00,016
Don't catch a cold as seasons are changing.

174
00:06:00,156 --> 00:06:01,316
Hang in there. You can do this!

175
00:06:01,586 --> 00:06:04,355
You know what? You know exactly what to say on TV now.

176
00:06:04,356 --> 00:06:05,385
"You can do this!"

177
00:06:05,386 --> 00:06:06,755
He's only been on five variety shows.

178
00:06:06,756 --> 00:06:08,525
Right. He said he was on only five variety shows.

179
00:06:08,526 --> 00:06:10,096
That's... Okay.

180
00:06:10,166 --> 00:06:12,465
- Honestly, I don't know much.
- Okay.

181
00:06:12,466 --> 00:06:14,065
But I just wanted to share this message.

182
00:06:14,066 --> 00:06:15,165
- That's so cool.
- This message...

183
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:16,605
- Really?
- I felt a sense of responsibility.

184
00:06:16,606 --> 00:06:17,665
For the test takers.

185
00:06:17,666 --> 00:06:18,765
Sure, I'm here for our movie.

186
00:06:18,766 --> 00:06:19,905
But I also feel a sense of responsibility.

187
00:06:19,906 --> 00:06:21,435
- After playing...
- Right.

188
00:06:21,436 --> 00:06:22,975
- the test writer in the movie?
- After your role?

189
00:06:22,976 --> 00:06:24,345
- After playing his role...
- They can catch up on the rest...

190
00:06:24,346 --> 00:06:25,676
- after the test.
- Right.

191
00:06:25,776 --> 00:06:27,615
- That's right.
- I just wanted to tell them that.

192
00:06:27,616 --> 00:06:30,015
Anyway, let's check where we're going today.

193
00:06:30,016 --> 00:06:31,115
Our schedule...

194
00:06:31,116 --> 00:06:32,655
Where are we going? I'm really curious.

195
00:06:32,656 --> 00:06:34,216
We need to check. All right.

196
00:06:34,486 --> 00:06:36,656
"Kim Yoon A, Kim Ga Yoon,"

197
00:06:36,826 --> 00:06:37,955
"and Lee Geon Woo."

198
00:06:37,956 --> 00:06:41,626
"We're running a publishing house which was founded six months ago."

199
00:06:41,726 --> 00:06:42,766
What?

200
00:06:42,866 --> 00:06:44,296
"As for our publishing house,"

201
00:06:44,766 --> 00:06:47,796
"we write everything by hand from the first page to the last."

202
00:06:47,896 --> 00:06:49,405
- What?
- What does this mean?

203
00:06:49,406 --> 00:06:51,305
- They write by hand?
- They're writing it by hand?

204
00:06:51,306 --> 00:06:52,876
- What?
- By hand?

205
00:06:53,076 --> 00:06:55,475
"When it's complete, we deliver it ourselves..."

206
00:06:55,476 --> 00:06:56,606
- "in person."
- What?

207
00:06:56,746 --> 00:06:57,746
- What?
- What?

208
00:06:58,046 --> 00:07:01,416
"We'd love to tell people about our handwritten books."

209
00:07:01,676 --> 00:07:02,915
"If we were to be on your show,"

210
00:07:02,916 --> 00:07:04,986
"would we get more readers?"

211
00:07:05,956 --> 00:07:08,956
I wonder if this publishing house sends out monthly issues...

212
00:07:09,286 --> 00:07:10,856
