213
00:07:11,326 --> 00:07:12,326
I don't know.

214
00:07:12,327 --> 00:07:13,526
Anyway, let's get going.

215
00:07:13,626 --> 00:07:15,155
I need to look it up. Hold on.

216
00:07:15,156 --> 00:07:17,425
- We must be there on time.
- We must be punctual.

217
00:07:17,426 --> 00:07:18,466
We should get going.

218
00:07:18,566 --> 00:07:20,295
- It's nine minutes away on foot.
- It's nearby.

219
00:07:20,296 --> 00:07:21,996
We can just double time it then.

220
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:23,465
I love walnut cakes.

221
00:07:23,466 --> 00:07:24,466
- Aren't they tasty?
- They're tasty.

222
00:07:24,467 --> 00:07:26,035
- They taste different down here.
- They're different.

223
00:07:26,036 --> 00:07:27,606
You need to get the original ones.

224
00:07:27,876 --> 00:07:28,935
The original ones...

225
00:07:28,936 --> 00:07:30,806
- Are they here?
- They're near Cheonan Station.

226
00:07:30,906 --> 00:07:32,375
- They're the first walnut cakes.
- It's still there.

227
00:07:32,376 --> 00:07:33,745
- They're the first walnut cakes.
- My gosh, seriously.

228
00:07:33,746 --> 00:07:34,915
She's indeed the honorary ambassador of Cheonan.

229
00:07:34,916 --> 00:07:35,985
- I really grew up...
- If you want to be an ambassador,

230
00:07:35,986 --> 00:07:37,016
- you must love Cheonan like her.
- She's the honorary ambassador.

231
00:07:37,186 --> 00:07:38,585
- Right.
- You must care as deeply as her.

232
00:07:38,586 --> 00:07:39,715
I was born here.

233
00:07:39,716 --> 00:07:41,886
- I also went to school here.
- Right.

234
00:07:42,256 --> 00:07:43,825
- I'm bound to love Cheonan.
- That makes sense.

235
00:07:43,826 --> 00:07:44,986
Yeon Seok, you're from Seoul. Right?

236
00:07:45,186 --> 00:07:47,025
I'm from Jinju, South Gyeongsang Province.

237
00:07:47,026 --> 00:07:48,455
- I went to school there.
- Jinju?

238
00:07:48,456 --> 00:07:49,465
- Jinju?
- Yes.

239
00:07:49,466 --> 00:07:51,025
Then I transferred to a school in Seoul.

240
00:07:51,026 --> 00:07:52,095
- I see.
- Yes.

241
00:07:52,096 --> 00:07:55,566
So my neighborhood was Gwangjin-gu.

242
00:07:56,106 --> 00:07:57,166
That was my turf.

243
00:07:57,236 --> 00:07:59,436
I'm really surprised right now.

244
00:07:59,706 --> 00:08:02,575
The roads at the intersection weren't paved before.

245
00:08:02,576 --> 00:08:04,805
- Really?
- They weren't paved like this.

246
00:08:04,806 --> 00:08:06,576
- They weren't paved?
- No.

247
00:08:06,676 --> 00:08:08,115
I have a lot of memories about this intersection.

248
00:08:08,116 --> 00:08:09,515
